+.. setting:: CONDITIONAL_REQUESTS_ENABLED
+
+CONDITIONAL_REQUESTS_ENABLED
+----------------------------
+
+Default: ``False``
+
+Whether the
+:class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.conditional.ConditionalRequestsMiddleware`
+is active.
+
+When enabled, Scrapy stores the ``ETag`` and ``Last-Modified`` validators of
+successful (``200 OK``) responses and, on subsequent requests for the same
+resource, sends ``If-None-Match`` and/or ``If-Modified-Since`` headers so
+that the origin server can answer ``304 Not Modified`` for unchanged
+resources, in which case the response is dropped before it reaches the
+spider.
+
+See :ref:`topics-dlmw-conditional-requests` for more information.
+
+.. setting:: CONDITIONAL_REQUESTS_DIR
+
+CONDITIONAL_REQUESTS_DIR
+------------------------
+
+Default: ``None``
+
+Directory used by the
+:class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.conditional.ConditionalRequestsMiddleware`
+to persist the validators of seen responses, so that later crawls, including
+crawls run in a different process, can send conditional requests for
+resources seen before.
+
+For each spider, a database file named
+``<spider name>_conditional_requests`` is created inside this directory. If
+the directory does not exist, it is created when the spider is opened.
+
+If not set, validators are only kept in memory and are lost when the crawl
+finishes.
+
